00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:53.900
With capital clearly rotating, let's examine the exact playbook investors are using right

00:01:53.900 --> 00:02:00.880
now. Intense rotational plays involve shifting capital between sectors or themes based on short-term

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:06.660
catalysts rather than long-term buy and hold. Today's data shows exactly why this matters.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:13.260
US tech funds posted record withdrawals while citizens upgraded Uber on Waymo momentum

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:18.720
and reiterated outperform ratings on national and PNN entertainment.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:25.380
The approach works by identifying where capital is rotating next using analyst target changes

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:29.080
and volume spikes instead of chasing yesterday's winners.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:35.680
Implemented by screening for stocks with fresh 12 month target increases from multiple brokers

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:41.340
and checking five day relative volume above 150% of the 20 day average

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:45.040
on platforms like interactive brokers or quest trade.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:51.520
Historically, rotations have delivered the strongest alpha in the final six to eight weeks of a quarter

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:57.600
when macro data shifts. They carry whipsaw risk if the catalyst fails to materialize.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.300
The key is requiring at least two confirming signals.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.140
Analyst action plus volume before committing capital.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:11.100
That same rotation logic is exactly why we're testing it live in today's practice

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:15.680
trade. This is a simulated trade for educational purposes only.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:20.680
Today's practice investment is Uber technologies on the NYSE.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:27.160
Citizens raised Uber's price target, citing accelerating Waymo Robotaxi growth momentum.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:32.840
