00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:37.020
of the 20 day moving average on volume above the 20 day average.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:44.620
The stop loss sits 6% below entry to account for continued AI-related rotation out of growth names.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:53.420
The target is plus 4% to plus 7% over the five day hold. Confidence is medium because we have two

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:58.740
confirming factors in the fresh analyst target raise plus sector rotation signals.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:05.180
This setup demonstrates how to use broker target revisions as a filter rather than a stand-alone

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:12.440
signal. It also shows the value of waiting for rotation into a name instead of chasing the prior

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:18.660
week's leaders. Before we check how yesterday's trade fared, here's the hard lesson it delivered.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:25.380
Last flash trade was MU on an AI momentum entry with volume confirmation.

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:36.540
We entered at $1,233 at market open and exited at $1,213.56 at market close.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:44.740
The position lost 1.58% or $15.77 on a $1,000 position.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:52.400
The earnings revision catalyst faded faster than expected once broader AI infrastructure cost concerns

00:04:52.400 --> 00:05:02.080
resurfaced. The trade lost 1.58% while the NASDAQ fell 0.5% on the same day for negative alpha of

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:10.020
1.08%. The new rule requires closing price confirmation before declaring any catalyst trade complete.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:17.000
That discipline pairs directly with understanding how ETFs can quietly cost you money at the open.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:30.520
Imagine you bought the new eFund HKEX Tech 100 index ETF ticker 3456 on its listing day at a 1.2%

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:38.660
premium to NAV because retail demand surged. Your order filled at that premium but the actual underlying

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:45.320
Hong Kong tech stocks traded flat. The mechanism that matters is the creation and redemption process.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:53.020
Authorized participants can create new ETF units by delivering the basket of stocks or redeem units for

00:05:53.020 --> 00:06:00.260
the underlying, which keeps the price within a tight band around NAV. When demand spikes, the premium

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:09.640
can widen to 1-2% intraday before arbitragers step in. That 1% difference on a $50,000 position equals

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:17.220
$500 left on the table if you sell before the premium compresses. Most retail investors don't realize

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:23.460
they can check real-time premium and discount data on the ETF issuer site or Bloomberg terminals

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:30.620
before placing a market order. The biggest mistake with new ETF launches is buying at the open without

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:38.360
checking the indicative NAV. Instead, always place a limit order at or below the last reported premium

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:48.020
level. While we're on tools, two new resources worth watching this week. The eFundHKEX Tech 100 index ETF

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:56.180
ticker 3456 tracks 100 Hong Kong listed technology companies and trades on the Hong Kong exchange.

00:06:56.900 --> 00:07:02.500
It gives Canadian investors direct exposure to the region without individual stock selection

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:09.660
and offers a low cost way to add emerging market tech diversification inside a TFSA.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:17.800
Use it via any broker with HKEX access, such as interactive brokers and compare its premium or

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:25.280
discount to NAV daily. The polymarket platform suffered a $2.9 million front end compromise

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:31.600
but contained the breach and will refund affected users. Active traders can treat polymarket

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:37.660
volumes as a sentiment gauge for macro events like rate decisions while keeping position sizes

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:44.940
tiny given custody and smart contract risks. A few more quick analysts moves to note before we wrap.

